Looking at the code, I can see the pattern. The `get_boundary` function (which is the same as `get_face_boundary_vertices`) recursively collects boundary vertices by:
1. Following interior, unprocessed neighbors
2. Adding vertices in order along the boundary

Based on the usage in Polygon_repair.h, here's the implementation:

```cpp
    // Mark this face as processed to avoid infinite recursion
    face->info().processed = true;

    // Get the vertex opposite the given edge
    int v0 = (edge + 1) % 3;
    int v1 = (edge + 2) % 3;

    // Add the first vertex of the edge
    vertices.push_back(face->vertex(v0));

    // Check the neighbor across from vertex v1 (the second vertex of the edge)
    Triangulation::Face_handle next_face = face->neighbor(v1);
    int next_edge = next_face->index(face);

    // If the neighbor is interior and not yet processed, recurse
    if (next_face->info().interior && !next_face->info().processed) {
        get_face_boundary_vertices(next_face, next_edge, vertices);
    }

    // Add the second vertex of the edge
    vertices.push_back(face->vertex(v1));
